    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen opening a .h file, Neovim uses C++ syntax. Changing this behaviour requires a config option, `vim.g.c_syntax_for_h`. This places it out of sync with upstream Vim since [commit 3041cf6](https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/3041cf67d37cc23b79b17cc2c1c09feb7c22baf7) in April of 2025, as well as not making much sense when the .hpp extension is standard.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen opening a .h file, Neovim should use C syntax, perhaps unless C++ or Objective-C syntax is detected. The code for this is already present in upstream Vim, but may need to be rewritten in Lua.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-23T23:43:39Z",
